# HENRI run-evidence: generated scaffold output (manifest is the evidence)
# Regenerable per-task files; M2_PART_I_EVIDENCE_BUNDLE.json records sha256+bytes
# for each. Ignoring them keeps generated output out of the repository AND avoids
# Windows MAX_PATH staging failures on the nested tasks/<task>/(export|summary).json
# paths -- a silent `git add` warning that once dropped 34 of 35 files.
# NOTE: rule placement matters. A parent-level negation cannot override the
# lower-level HENRI V2/.gitignore '*.jsonl' rule, so these must live here.
experiments/verification/scicode-instrument-control*/
experiments/verification/m2-agent-loop-*/
experiments/verification/m2-rest-end-to-end*/
experiments/verification/runs/
